# Line endings are CONTENT in this repository, not formatting.
#
# Several migrations modify an existing function by fetching
# pg_get_functiondef() and doing exact text replacement on the result. That is
# how the kitchen release path and the recommendation ranker are changed
# without forking a two-hundred-line body into a new file and letting the two
# copies drift apart.
#
# A CRLF checkout breaks it: the search literal inside the migration gains
# carriage returns while the function body stored in the database does not, so
# every replace() matches nothing. Each rewrite asserts that it matched and
# raises if it did not, so the failure is loud rather than silent — but the
# point of this file is that it should not happen at all.
#
# Found the hard way, and verified by forcing every .sql file to CRLF and
# watching the test harness refuse to boot.
*.sql text eol=lf

# The harness reads those files; keep it consistent.
*.mjs text eol=lf
